---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
  title="KRaft Consensus Quorum"
  description="Native Rust KRaft consensus implementation, state machines, and KIP-595 wire compatibility."
  currentSlug="/docs/kraft"
>
  <div class="space-y-6">
    <div class="border-b border-white/10 pb-4">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white sm:text-4xl">KRaft Consensus Quorum</h1>
      <p class="text-gray-400 mt-2 text-base">
        Metadata consensus without ZooKeeper via <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">crabka-raft</code> and <code class="font-mono text-krab-300">crabka-kraft-core</code>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-sm text-gray-300">
      <p>
        Krabka metadata is managed by a native KRaft quorum implementing KIP-595. Active controllers accept metadata write RPCs (<code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">CreateTopics</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">AlterPartition</code>, <code class="font-mono text-xs text-gray-200">CreatePartitions</code>), serialize them as records into the <code class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300">@metadata</code> partition, and replicate them to follower controllers.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white pt-2">Features</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-2 text-gray-400 pl-2">
        <li><strong>Zero-Copy Snapshots:</strong> Periodically truncates metadata logs into memory-mapped snapshot files.</li>
        <li><strong>Voter Sets:</strong> Modeled cleanly in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300">crabka-voters</code> with dynamic reconfigurations.</li>
        <li><strong>Down-Conversion:</strong> Legacy v0/v1 message-set codecs in <code class="font-mono text-xs text-krab-300">crabka-records-legacy</code> ensure old clients communicate without disruption.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
